WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.620
- Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:02.700
This is hilarious.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.200
Meet Scarlet.
Have y'all met before?

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.132
- I have not met Scarlett
Johansson before.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:08.550
I have just watched her on award shows,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.980
periodically saving
the universe, you know?

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.420
- [Kelly] Yes.
- Thank you for your service.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.253
- My pleasure.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.250
- So what's the ambassador
prune thing. What?

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.320
- Okay, so I am from a little farm town

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.400
in Northern California

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.380
that is the prune capital of the world.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.710
And when you are sort of like
a "thinky," liberal, gay guy

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.600
you don't always get to
have a great relationship

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.550
with your conservative little farm town.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.050
- Okay.
- So I would periodically

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.881
just tweet at the California Prune Board,

00:00:32.881 --> 00:00:36.660
"I should be your unofficial,
official ambassador."

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.555
And then finally I said, "Hey,
if you guys don't respond

00:00:39.555 --> 00:00:43.024
I'm taking my talents to the
California Cling Peach Board."

00:00:43.024 --> 00:00:44.003
They were like, "Fine.

00:00:44.003 --> 00:00:47.115
We give in, you can be our ambassador."

00:00:47.115 --> 00:00:48.715
- [Kelly] Here's the thing.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.540
I don't think I've ever had a prune.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.100
- Prunes are delicious.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:53.933
They are jamming.

00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:55.003
They are sophisticated.

00:00:55.003 --> 00:00:57.000
French people go crazy for them.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.983
Am I right, Scarlett Johansson?

00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:00.540
- Oui, absolutely.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.373
- [Crew member] Take a pack?

00:01:01.373 --> 00:01:04.417
- We put together a lovely
prune sampler for you guys.

00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:06.214
- Oh my goodness.

00:01:06.214 --> 00:01:08.160
- Wait a minute, can I ask you a kind of

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.600
like a question that I
should probably know?

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.433
- [Guy] Absolutely.

00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:12.570
- Is a prune...it's a plum right?

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.387
- In California, like a
prune is just a dried plum.

00:01:15.387 --> 00:01:16.220
- Oh, I love plums.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.730
- And like everybody loves plums.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.620
Everybody understands like an apricot.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.330
It just turns into a dried apricot

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.944
but they get weirded out when
you go from plum to prune.

00:01:24.944 --> 00:01:26.490
- Oh.
- And it's just

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.559
the same delicious
flavor but concentrated.

00:01:28.559 --> 00:01:31.320
- Okay. You're a great ambassador.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.370
- I love prunes.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.203
I'm sorry.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.912
I'm really proud of my little farm town.

00:01:36.912 --> 00:01:40.011
We produce tons of almonds and peaches.

00:01:40.011 --> 00:01:41.010
- [Kelly] I love all those.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.120
- It's a great place.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.120
I just wish it were more
okay to be, you know,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.992
gay or a woman or a person of color there.

00:01:46.992 --> 00:01:50.325
(Kelly laughing loudly)

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.825
- That was an enormous amount of people.

00:01:53.825 --> 00:01:55.500
(Guy laughing boisterously)

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.910
- [Kelly] So wait, you're also an author.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:57.743
Here we go.

00:01:57.743 --> 00:01:59.130
So "My Life as a Goddess."

00:01:59.130 --> 00:01:59.963
Where did this come from?

00:01:59.963 --> 00:02:00.975
Why'd you wanna do this?

00:02:00.975 --> 00:02:03.106
(audience clapping)

00:02:03.106 --> 00:02:05.340
- I just, I had this
story that I would always

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.173
tell my friends.

00:02:06.173 --> 00:02:09.150
There's a story from Greek
mythology about a lady,

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.670
a goddess, who was pregnant,
but didn't have a husband.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.410
And people were like mean
to her and made fun of her.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:16.170
And she like got like mad and
pissed off and walked away.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.120
And then she was like,
"Oh, wait, I'm a goddess,"

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.490
and then turned around and
turned them all into frogs.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:24.180
And I think that that's an
important thing to remember is

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.033
that you have amazing powers.

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:28.643
Like we all have amazing
powers that we can use.

00:02:28.643 --> 00:02:30.570
And when you're down on
yourself, you need to

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.030
remember to use those powers
in whatever way you can.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:33.990
- [Kelly] And don't give it away.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:34.823
- Don't give it away.

00:02:34.823 --> 00:02:37.296
- Yeah. I love that they all are frogs.

00:02:37.296 --> 00:02:38.310
(Kelly and Guy laughing)

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.990
So you, you said this a while back.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.510
Some people just need to find a path

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.790
to being comfortable
with themselves enough

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.680
that they can be comfortable
with people around.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.320
I love this quote because
I think that's so true.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.004
Until you're comfortable with
yourself and in your own skin,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.640
how, first of all can anybody
else be comfortable with you?

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.620
And then also it's reciprocal.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.453
I love this.

00:02:56.453 --> 00:02:57.510
Why do, why do you think this?

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.730
- I think it's so real
that anytime somebody has

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.160
a weird relationship
to your specificities,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.908
for me so frequently
being gay and very fat.

00:03:04.908 --> 00:03:07.080
And it's like, that's not about me.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.100
That's about them.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.407
You know, it's about their
issues with themselves.

00:03:10.407 --> 00:03:13.680
And I think that one of
the best things we can do

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.690
for other people is respect ourselves

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.994
and our own specificities enough

00:03:16.994 --> 00:03:19.140
to be able to respect theirs.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.330
And that's really what this
movie "Bros" is about is

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.910
like two white, cis gay
guys who have developed

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.015
like protective mechanisms for dealing

00:03:26.015 --> 00:03:29.130
with a homophobic world
who don't realize how

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.830
much those protective mechanisms
are hurting themselves

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:34.110
and the people around them and
then learning to like chill

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.450
out and have fun and be
comfortable with themselves.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.283
- Yeah.
- But also,

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.430
as I was saying before, Kelly Clarkson

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.570
I have to tell you

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:40.710
- Okay.
- Thank you so much

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.140
for how much you have taken
care of me on dance floors.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.920
So many times in my life when
I needed you, you showed up.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.612
- Well, you're gonna love the next album.

00:03:48.612 --> 00:03:49.920
(laughs boisterously)

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.810
- [Kelly] Wait. So most, most of the cast

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:55.650
in production team of
"Bros" were LGBTQ, right?

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.483
- [Guy] Yes.

00:03:56.483 --> 00:03:57.316
- [Kelly] That's important.

00:03:57.316 --> 00:03:58.290
- [Guy] The entire cast,
whether they're playing

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.390
straight people or queer
people or trans people

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.920
or LGBTQ plus.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.460
We have a couple of
cameos from iconic divas,

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:08.790
who I believe are part
of the plus in LGBTQ+

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.920
you know, you guys have given us so much

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.643
and we owe so much back to you.

00:04:12.643 --> 00:04:14.580
- I love you so much.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.770
Okay. So wait, we know
that Scarlett is really

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.040
into music, and you're great
at hosting a game show.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.080
So like, what if we did a game

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.633
like a music game and you host
it, would you be into this?

00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:25.290
- I mean, that sounds really fun.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.673
- Okay, I'm into it. Okay.

